## What the product does now, by id (one line each)
- Capture: screen + camera + mic + tab/system audio armed together at one epoch; instant start; chips toggle any input mid-take (a real stop and a new segment); pause/resume exist in the engine with no UI (F6); every stop drains every file (P0-tail); a stop past its 5 s budget keeps what reached disk (H5); a device that dies or never delivers is said live and stamped in Recording.lost (H4); an encoder/worker/recorder death closes the segment and opens the next, ≤4 per channel (H1); the disk guard reads real storage growth and auto-stops before the disk fills (B5); the first VideoEncoder per launch is warmed at mount so a take killed at 2 s keeps ~1 s of picture after the first page load (H6), and the same warm METERS this machine AT THE DISPLAY'S OWN SIZE with the take's own codec (B14 2026-09-03) — what a take may attempt at 60 fps is decided from that reading, which carries the frame it was taken at, and a reading taken SMALLER than the surface understates it and may no longer refuse anything; the record press also opens THE ON-TOP PANEL (U1, `?panel=0` off) — a Document Picture-in-Picture window above every other app carrying the timer, the audio ring, Stop and Pause/Continue, closed with the take, absent on any browser without the API.
- Elastic: BIASED UP since E2 (Robert's 09-02 ruling, in the engine). Order of defence, enforced not assumed: (1) the unseen work is shed at `serious` (background brake) → (2) the encoder's byte-bounded burst absorber holds up to 4 frames it used to drop → (3) the picture steps LAST, only at `critical`, only when the take's OWN work is what is critical (`ownLevel` — a machine busy in another window never costs Robert his rate), and only after (1). Up on one confirming sample (~500 ms), widening only for a climb that was undone; a probe at 15 s that no reading may veto, so a wrong reading can never pin a take. Pressure is read PER HARDWARE BLOCK (encoder/cpu/gpu/disk; gpu and disk read `unmeasured`, honestly). SINCE J6 THE READING COMES FROM THE RAW SCREEN CHANNEL'S ENCODER, not the composite's: the composite no longer encodes, and a detector fed the cost of a 0.4 ms draw would call a drowning machine nominal. Same detector, same sampler (M1's shared seam), same `notePressure` — the instrument moved to the encoder that is still there. Every shed and recovery is in the take (`stopStats.elastic`) and graded (`elastic` dimension). ELASTIC COVERS MAX AND IS SWITCHED OFF THERE, WHICH IS NOT THE SAME AS MAX NOT HAVING IT — Robert 2026-09-03, correcting this line twice: "elastic must work for max, it is just now turned off so we polish max without it" · "MAX ELASTIC OFF UNTIL I SAY SO" · "until i say so". ONE system, max inside it, the picture step off there until he moves it (`?maxladder=1` inside max, `?floor=1` for M1's floor). Since 2026-09-03 the max STEP actually reaches max MODE (it never did — the slider wrote only `inout.quality.step`), so a max take is no longer refused before it starts and no longer steps mid-take: measured on a max+camera take, before/after on one build, 3 encoders (490 Mpx/s, composite dropping 84 of 307 frames, ladder stepping 60→30 at "pressure critical, encode-latency 365.5 ms", card RED on rate) → 2 encoders (366 Mpx/s, no composite, nothing stepped, card GREEN 13/13). A max take sheds nothing and drops frames where they fall, by his choice and until he says otherwise. M1 BUILT the same system for it behind `?floor=1` (OFF) — the detector reading from the raw screen encoder's own worker through one shared sampler (`capture/pressureSampler.ts`), the unseen work shed first, then the camera's rate, then the screen's 60→30, same `ladderDecision`, back in reverse as the machine eases; measured engaging 841 ms after a load and returning 895 ms after it lifts. The SIZE is its last rung (`?floorres=`, also off: a 5,047 ms seam under load against 30 ms idle — a measurement, not a rule; the order is rate first, resolution after, DECISIONS robert (22)).
