- THE DOOR (M1, 2026-09-03): every change to rate, resolution, quality or which channels run passes through `core/door.ts`, and passing through it is how the change is made — the caller cannot reach the primitive without a ticket only that call can mint. Applied / refused / failed, with what it was measured on and who decided it, into `stopStats.decisions`, mirrored into E2's ledger for the three defence layers, graded by the card's `decisions` dimension, carried into every export's certification as `capture.gaveUp`, and readable mid-take. A test scans the shipped source: `applyConstraints` exists in ONE file, `noteElastic` in two, every `encoder.configure` is an allowlisted entry that says why it is not a dial — a new fallback that bypasses the door fails the build. Chrome's own capture adaptation cannot be owned, so it is DETECTED at 1 Hz and recorded like everything else.
